# apps/web JSDoc / comments

Source of truth: `.agents/skills/jsdoc-typescript-docs/SKILL.md`

## Must

- Use `/** JSDoc */` for public APIs and exported types; use `//` for implementation “why” notes.
- Write method summaries as third-person verb phrases (“Returns…”, “Normalizes…”).
- Put each JSDoc tag on its own line.
- Document parameters/returns only when they add meaning beyond the TypeScript signature.
- Use repeated `//` for multi-line ordinary comments — never `/* */` blocks.

## Must not

- Put TypeScript types in `@param` / `@returns` / `@property` tags.
- Add redundant `@type` comments on `useState` or other obvious locals.
- Restate only the symbol name in documentation.
